/* ============================================================================
   Cluck Wars — UI Toolkit theme (menu front-end)
   Look: Direction A "Barnyard Toybox" with painted-wood trim (spec
   docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-menu-ui-overhaul.md, "Visual system").
   The values below are the tokens in CluckWarsTokens.uss (Direction A block),
   written out literally because this sheet is attached per page template and
   a :root custom property is not guaranteed to reach it:
       ink #2a1a0c   cream #fff8e8 / inset #f3e6c8   gold #f5c842 / edge #d9a521
       CTA green #7be35c -> #36a82c   wood #8a5a2e / #7a4a22
   Three value steps: the backdrop (MenuUiController backdrop, tinted per page),
   wood panels (PanelFrame / CardBg 9-slices), raised cream cards with ink text.
   Button rule: ONE green CTA per screen (the forward action); gold means
   selection / "you" only; wood means navigation and frames.

   Display type (Lilita One: titles, buttons, ribbons) carries a thick ink
   -unity-text-outline plus a hard text-shadow. Both were verified to render on
   Unity 6000.3 in an off-screen capture on 2026-10-06 (the old "no
   text-shadow" ban dated from an older branch). Still NOT available: box-shadow,
   gap, linear-gradient, inherit - depth comes from the baked atoms
   (ButtonGrayscale bevel, GlossOverlay, PanelFrame/CardBg/CardGlowFrame
   9-slices) and rounded corners are border-radius + overflow:hidden.
   Class/ability colors & the chicken sprite are applied in C# at bind time
   (MenuUiController). Fonts are set on the root in C# (UiGfx.ChunkyFont) as a
   guaranteed fallback; url() font refs below are the primary path.

   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   MOBILE SIZING CONTRACT  (2026-07-23 Android pass) — READ BEFORE EDITING
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Android is the primary target and the app is landscape-locked
   (ProjectSettings: autorotate portrait = 0). Assets/Resources/PanelSettings
   is ScaleWithScreenSize, reference 1920x1080, MatchWidthOrHeight 0.5, so

       scale = sqrt((screenW / 1920) * (screenH / 1080))

   On phones, pixel density rises with resolution, so `scale * 160 / ppi`
   lands in a tight band whatever the handset:

       Pixel 9        2424x1080 @422ppi   scale 1.124   0.426 dp per px
       1344p flagship 2992x1344 @486ppi   scale 1.392   0.458 dp per px
       budget 720p    1600x720  @270ppi   scale 0.745   0.441 dp per px

   => 1 dp ~= 2.35 USS px on this canvas.  Derived floors, which every rule
   below respects:

       touch target   48 dp  ->  116 px   (min-height AND min-width)
       body / button  16 sp  ->   38 px
       readable text  14 sp  ->   34 px   <- hard floor for anything load-bearing
       caption        12 sp  ->   30 px   <- decorative / secondary only

   The pre-2026-07-23 sheet used 9–20 px type and ~40–70 px controls, i.e.
   4–9 sp text and 17–30 dp targets — roughly a third of the Android minimum.
   Consequence of the fix: on a 1920x1080 desktop window the menu renders
   chunky rather than dense. That is deliberate; the phone is the target and
   the arcade art style carries it. Do NOT "fix" it by shrinking type — shrink
   the PanelSettings reference resolution only if you re-derive this table
   AND re-check Assets/UI/Styles/TouchControls.uss, whose HIT TARGETS are
   already phone-correct (150 px hex = 64 dp, joystick base 280 px = 119 dp)
   and would break if the reference moved. (Its *type* was not fine — the hex
   label was 6.4 sp and the slot badge 8.5 sp until the 2026-07-23 sweep.)

   This contract governs every surface, not just this sheet:
     Assets/UI/Styles/MatchTopBar.uss    glanceable HUD, 30-52 px
     Assets/UI/Styles/MatchOverlays.uss  full-screen modals, 34 px floor
     Assets/UI/Styles/TouchControls.uss  targets 150 px, type 28-46 px
     MatchHud.cs      UGUI Canvas — same ScaleWithScreenSize 1920x1080 @0.5
     DebugHud.cs      IMGUI — no scaler exists, so it scales GUI.matrix by dpi
   ============================================================================ */

/* ---- Screen root + pages -------------------------------------------------- */
/* Transparent since stage 2: every page sits on the shared backdrop that
   MenuUiController puts behind all of them (.cw-backdrop below). */
.cw-screen {
    flex-grow: 1;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    overflow: hidden;
    align-items: stretch;
    justify-content: flex-start;
}
.cw-page { flex-grow: 1; align-items: stretch; justify-content: flex-start; }
.cw-hidden { display: none; }

/* ---- Typography ----------------------------------------------------------- */
/* Headings stay on one line (nowrap) so ribbons/badges grow to fit instead of
   wrapping like the old UGUI ("CHA / RACT"). Body text wraps normally.
   Sizes follow the ramp in the mobile sizing contract above. */
.cw-title, .cw-heading, .cw-label {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    color: rgb(254, 245, 224);               /* #fef5e0 */
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    white-space: nowrap;
}

/* Display treatment: thick ink outline + hard drop shadow. Shared by every
   Lilita One element that sits on art or on a coloured face (titles, ribbons,
   buttons, cast names, panel headings). Not used for ink text on cream -
   an ink outline on ink text only thickens it. */
.cw-title, .cw-heading, .cw-label, .cw-btn, .cw-home-btn, .cw-mini-btn,
.cw-menu-cast__name, .cw-deck-group__title, .cw-sheet__title, .cw-menu-playagain__label {
    -unity-text-outline-width: 4px;
    -unity-text-outline-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    text-shadow: 0px 5px 0px rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.85);
}
/* UI Toolkit draws the outline TMP-style, half of it INSIDE the glyph, so a
   width that suits 84 px type would eat 30 px type. Measured on 2026-10-06:
   6 px on titles, 4 px on buttons/headings, 3 px below ~36 px. */
.cw-title { -unity-text-outline-width: 6px; text-shadow: 0px 8px 0px rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.9); }
.cw-menu-cast__name, .cw-deck-group__title { -unity-text-outline-width: 3px; text-shadow: 0px 3px 0px rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.85); }

/* Body text that sits directly on the backdrop art (not on a card): a thin
   ink outline is what keeps it legible over the painted plate. */
.cw-on-art {
    color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
    -unity-text-outline-width: 2px;
    -unity-text-outline-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    text-shadow: 0px 3px 0px rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.8);
}
.cw-title   { font-size: 84px; letter-spacing: 4px; }   /* 36 sp */
.cw-heading { font-size: 48px; letter-spacing: 2px; }   /* 20 sp */
.cw-label   { font-size: 40px; }                        /* 17 sp */

.cw-body {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 34px;                                    /* 14 sp — the floor */
    color: rgb(196, 160, 96);                /* #c4a060 secondary */
    white-space: normal;
}

.cw-accent    { color: rgb(245, 200, 66); }  /* #f5c842 */
.cw-text-dark { color: rgb(26, 14, 4); }

/* ---- Backdrop (one element behind every page) ------------------------------
   MenuUiController puts #Backdrop + #BackdropTint behind the page host and, per
   page, adds ONE scene modifier class (MenuUiController.BackdropFor). Phase 2:
   one golden-hour farm, four views (Art/UI/Backgrounds/Bg_*.png, 2880x1440 with a
   centred 16:9 safe area); scale-and-crop keeps the centre on 4:3 and 20:9. The
   base rule keeps the old barn plate as the fallback for a page with no scene. */
.cw-backdrop {
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Backgrounds/MenuBackground.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-and-crop;
}
.cw-backdrop--main    { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Backgrounds/Bg_MainMenu.png"); }
.cw-backdrop--class   { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Backgrounds/Bg_ClassSelect.png"); }
.cw-backdrop--loadout { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Backgrounds/Bg_Loadout.png"); }
.cw-backdrop--lobby   { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Backgrounds/Bg_Lobby.png"); }
/* Over the scene: an ink vignette (Atoms/Vignette.png, clear centre, ~60% ink in
   the corners) plus a per-page colour set in C# - a light ink scrim, or the class
   wash on PICK YOUR BIRD. Text that sits directly on the art does NOT rely on this
   for contrast: it gets an ink plate (.cw-art-plate) instead. */
.cw-backdrop-tint {
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
    background-color: rgba(26, 13, 4, 0.10);
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/Vignette.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
}
/* Ink plate for text that sits directly on the bright scenes (subtitle, solo hint,
   cast names, lobby HOUSE RULES). Measured against the brightest pixel of each Bg_*
   (pure white sun, after the 10% scrim): 78% ink composites to ~#54473a, cream text on
   it is 8.2:1 and the light class names 4.1-8.0:1 (30 px Lilita = large text, 3:1). */
.cw-art-plate {
    background-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.78);
    border-top-left-radius: 14px; border-top-right-radius: 14px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 14px; border-bottom-right-radius: 14px;
    padding-left: 18px; padding-right: 18px; padding-top: 2px; padding-bottom: 6px;
}
/* Safe-area host: every page lives inside it; MenuUiController.ApplySafeArea
   pads it from Screen.safeArea so nothing lands under a notch or the gesture
   bar while the backdrop still bleeds to the screen edges. */
.cw-page-host { flex-grow: 1; }

/* ---- Value steps: wood panel / cream card / inset --------------------------
   Wood panel = PanelFrame 9-slice (96 px corners at half scale). */
/* Phase 2: painted plank panel (Frames/Frame_WoodPanel, 9-slice 40, gold-leaf edge, nails). */
.cw-wood-panel {
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Frames/Frame_WoodPanel.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    -unity-slice-left: 40; -unity-slice-right: 40; -unity-slice-top: 40; -unity-slice-bottom: 40;
    -unity-slice-scale: 1px;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
}
/* Dark wood well = CardBg 9-slice (the pick rows on the loadout). */
.cw-wood-well {
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/CardBg.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    -unity-slice-left: 56; -unity-slice-right: 56; -unity-slice-top: 56; -unity-slice-bottom: 56;
    -unity-slice-scale: 0.5px;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
}
/* Raised cream card (Phase 2: Frames/Card_Cream 9-slice 40/40/40/44 - ink outline, top
   highlight, bottom bevel and a soft drop shadow in a 10 px transparent margin). The
   outline is in the art, so the element carries no border of its own. */
.cw-raised {
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Frames/Card_Cream.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    -unity-slice-left: 40; -unity-slice-right: 40; -unity-slice-top: 40; -unity-slice-bottom: 44;
    -unity-slice-scale: 0.75px;
    border-left-width: 0; border-right-width: 0; border-top-width: 0; border-bottom-width: 0;
}
/* Inset well on a cream card. */
.cw-inset {
    background-color: rgb(243, 230, 200);
    border-left-width: 3px; border-right-width: 3px; border-top-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-left-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.35); border-right-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.35);
    border-top-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.35); border-bottom-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.35);
    border-top-left-radius: 14px; border-top-right-radius: 14px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 14px; border-bottom-right-radius: 14px;
}
/* Selection glow = CardGlowFrame 9-slice as an overlay child that bleeds just
   outside its card. Hidden unless the parent is selected (class chips) or the
   controller adds it (picked ability card, your lobby card). The ring sits at
   52/400 of the source, so at slice-scale 0.6 an inset of -27 puts it ~4 px
   outside the card's ink border. First child, picking ignored. */
.cw-glow {
    position: absolute; left: -27px; top: -27px; right: -27px; bottom: -27px;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/CardGlowFrame.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    -unity-slice-left: 72; -unity-slice-right: 72; -unity-slice-top: 72; -unity-slice-bottom: 72;
    -unity-slice-scale: 0.6px;
}

/* Ink text steps for cream surfaces (contrast on #fff8e8 / #f3e6c8):
   ink ~16:1, soft brown ~7:1 - both clear 4.5:1. */
.cw-ink       { color: rgb(42, 26, 12); }
.cw-ink-soft  { color: rgb(107, 74, 42); }

/* Reduced motion: the root carries .cw-reduced-motion while
   PlayerPreferences.ReducedMotionEnabled is on, which zeroes every hover/press
   scale transition and selection pop in the menus. */
/* Doubled class: (0,2,0) beats every single-class rule that sets its own duration (.cw-class-tile,
   .cw-slot-box, .cw-perk-badge, .cw-pagewrap, ...), which a bare .cw-reduced-motion * (0,1,0) lost to by order. */
.cw-reduced-motion.cw-reduced-motion * { transition-duration: 0s; }
.cw-reduced-motion .cw-btn:hover, .cw-reduced-motion .cw-btn:active,
.cw-reduced-motion .cw-home-btn:hover, .cw-reduced-motion .cw-home-btn:active,
.cw-reduced-motion .cw-ability-card:hover, .cw-reduced-motion .cw-perk-badge:hover,
.cw-reduced-motion .cw-class-tile:hover { scale: 1 1; }

/* ---- Glossy surfaces ------------------------------------------------------ */
.cw-panel {
    background-color: rgb(58, 34, 16);        /* #3a2210 */
    border-left-width: 4px; border-right-width: 4px; border-top-width: 4px; border-bottom-width: 4px;
    border-left-color: rgb(138, 106, 58); border-right-color: rgb(138, 106, 58);
    border-top-color: rgb(138, 106, 58); border-bottom-color: rgb(138, 106, 58);
    border-top-left-radius: 22px; border-top-right-radius: 22px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 22px; border-bottom-right-radius: 22px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/GlossOverlay.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
}

.cw-card {
    background-color: rgb(58, 40, 22);        /* #3a2816 */
    border-left-width: 3px; border-right-width: 3px; border-top-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-left-color: rgb(106, 74, 40); border-right-color: rgb(106, 74, 40);
    border-top-color: rgb(106, 74, 40); border-bottom-color: rgb(106, 74, 40);
    border-top-left-radius: 18px; border-top-right-radius: 18px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 18px; border-bottom-right-radius: 18px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/GlossOverlay.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    transition-property: scale; transition-duration: 0.12s;
}
.cw-card--selected { scale: 1.04 1.04; }

/* ---- Buttons -------------------------------------------------------------- */
/* The Stage-0 ButtonGrayscale atom (9-slice 52) is a beveled glossy pill, tinted
   per-variant at runtime — replaces flat bg-color + Gloss + colored borders.
   No element border (the bevel is baked); tint colours are pushed brighter than
   the target since -unity-background-image-tint-color multiplies the ~grey face.
   min-height/min-width hold the 48 dp Android touch floor even when a caller
   overrides font-size or padding inline. */
.cw-btn {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 40px;
    color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    min-height: 116px; min-width: 116px;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);   /* clear the default runtime-Button grey */
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/ButtonGrayscale.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    -unity-background-image-tint-color: rgb(171, 111, 57);
    border-left-width: 0; border-right-width: 0; border-top-width: 0; border-bottom-width: 0;
    padding-top: 20px; padding-bottom: 26px; padding-left: 44px; padding-right: 44px;
    transition-property: scale; transition-duration: 0.10s;
}
.cw-btn:hover  { scale: 1.03 1.03; }
.cw-btn:active { scale: 0.97 0.97; }
/* ONE BUTTON-COLOUR RULE (spec "Visual system"):
     green   the single forward action on a screen - PLAY SOLO, GEAR UP, READY,
             START MATCH. Tint is the CTA ramp #7be35c -> #36a82c divided by the
             atom's ~0.81 grey face so the bevel lands on the ramp.
     wood    navigation and secondary actions (HOME/BACK, gear, HOST/JOIN,
             ability lab, share/copy). #8a5a2e pushed the same way.
     gold    selection / "you" only - never a button.
   Labels are cream with the display ink outline on every face, which is what
   keeps them above 4.5:1 regardless of the face colour. */
/* Phase 2 art: green = the painted CTA plank (Frames/Frame_CtaPlank, 9-slice 48/36/48/40,
   untinted); wood = the plank panel (Frames/Frame_WoodPanel, 9-slice 40) at 0.6 so its nails
   and gold-leaf edge stay small on a button. The plank's 3D lip is at the bottom, so labels sit
   a little high (padding-bottom > padding-top). */
.cw-btn--green {
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Frames/Frame_CtaPlank.png");
    -unity-slice-left: 48; -unity-slice-right: 48; -unity-slice-top: 36; -unity-slice-bottom: 40;
    -unity-slice-scale: 1px;
    -unity-background-image-tint-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);
    padding-top: 18px; padding-bottom: 28px;
}
.cw-btn--wood, .cw-btn--neutral {
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Frames/Frame_WoodPanel.png");
    -unity-slice-left: 40; -unity-slice-right: 40; -unity-slice-top: 40; -unity-slice-bottom: 40;
    -unity-slice-scale: 0.6px;
    -unity-background-image-tint-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);
}
/* A disabled primary must still read as text, not as a ghost - 40% opacity on
   cream over the face drops under 4.5:1. Dim the face, keep the outlined label. */
.cw-btn:disabled { opacity: 1; -unity-background-image-tint-color: rgb(150, 140, 128); color: rgb(236, 226, 206); }

/* Focus ring for D-pad/keyboard navigation on the shared button atoms (their
   border is 0 at rest, so this never fights the resting look). Slot boxes and
   perk badges are left out on purpose: a real tap focuses a Button, and a cream
   focus border would hide their gold armed/selected border. */
.cw-btn:focus, .cw-home-btn:focus {
    border-left-width: 5px; border-right-width: 5px; border-top-width: 5px; border-bottom-width: 5px;
    border-left-color: rgb(254, 245, 224); border-right-color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
    border-top-color: rgb(254, 245, 224); border-bottom-color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
}

/* Home/back button — absolutely placed at a header's top-left, leaves the
   centered ribbon undisturbed. */
.cw-home-btn {
    position: absolute; left: 28px; top: 10px;   /* the wood plank fills its whole 116 px box (Phase 2) */
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 36px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    /* 124, not the 116 floor: the plank art sits inside transparent bevel margins, and the
       VISIBLE plank has to clear 48 dp on a Pixel 9 too (re-audit item 18). */
    min-height: 124px; min-width: 200px;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Frames/Frame_WoodPanel.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    -unity-slice-left: 40; -unity-slice-right: 40; -unity-slice-top: 40; -unity-slice-bottom: 40;
    -unity-slice-scale: 0.6px;
    border-left-width: 0; border-right-width: 0; border-top-width: 0; border-bottom-width: 0;
    padding-top: 16px; padding-bottom: 20px; padding-left: 30px; padding-right: 30px;
    transition-property: scale; transition-duration: 0.1s;
}
.cw-home-btn:hover  { scale: 1.04 1.04; }
.cw-home-btn:active { scale: 0.96 0.96; }
/* Gear (settings) - same wood atom, mirrored to the top-right, square, and the
   gear is the Glyph_Gear sprite (no emoji font). Accessible name = its tooltip,
   resolved from settings.title by UiText.ResolveTree. */
.cw-gear-btn {
    left: auto; right: 28px;
    min-width: 124px; width: 124px; height: 124px;
    padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 6px;
    align-items: center; justify-content: center;
}
.cw-gear-btn__icon {
    width: 80px; height: 80px;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Icons/Glyph_Gear.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
}

/* ---- Ribbon --------------------------------------------------------------- */
/* The Stage-0 Ribbon atom is a grayscale banner-with-tails (9-slice 92,32),
   tinted gold at runtime — replaces the flat gold bar + Gloss sheen. The 92px
   side borders are the fixed tails, so content padding clears them. */
/* Painted-wood ribbon (spec: wood for frames and ribbons; gold is selection
   only). Tint = wood #8a5a2e pushed for the ~0.78 grey face. Title is cream
   with the display outline, not ink-on-gold any more. */
/* Phase 2: Frames/Frame_Ribbon (768x160, horizontal 3-slice 168/0/168/0, untinted wood).
   Height is fixed at 104 px so the tails scale uniformly (0.65 = 104/160 -> 109 px tails)
   and only the plank stretches. The plank's text band is y 15-121 of 160 (~10-79 px here),
   so the label sits above centre: more padding at the bottom than the top. */
.cw-ribbon {
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Frames/Frame_Ribbon.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    -unity-slice-left: 168; -unity-slice-right: 168; -unity-slice-top: 0; -unity-slice-bottom: 0;
    -unity-slice-scale: 0.65px;
    height: 104px; flex-shrink: 0;
    padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 20px; padding-left: 124px; padding-right: 124px;
    align-items: center; justify-content: center;
}
.cw-ribbon .cw-title { color: rgb(254, 245, 224); font-size: 52px; letter-spacing: 3px; -unity-text-outline-width: 5px; text-shadow: 0px 4px 0px rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.85); padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; }

/* ============================================================================
   MAIN MENU  (2026-07-24 redesign — see Assets/UI/MainMenu.uxml for the why)
   Vertical budget on the 1080 canvas, distributed by the flex spacers in the
   page rather than by fixed offsets, so the block stays centred on any aspect:
       title block   ~230   cast band ~300   actions ~330   build stamp ~40
   ============================================================================ */
/* Painted farmyard-arena plate (Flux, 1344x768) behind the whole menu.
   scale-and-crop, NOT stretch-to-fill: the plate is 16:9 and the canvas is
   16:9, but a phone's safe area is not, and stretching a painted background
   is instantly visible where the fence lines skew. */
/* The plate itself moved to the shared backdrop (.cw-backdrop) in stage 2, and
   the flat dark scrim that used to knock it back was replaced by the per-page
   warm lift (.cw-backdrop-tint): legibility now comes from the display outline
   on every word that sits on the art, not from darkening the art. */
.cw-menu { align-items: center; justify-content: center; }

.cw-menu-titleblock { align-items: center; flex-shrink: 0; }
.cw-menu-title    { font-size: 128px; letter-spacing: 8px; }
/* Lighter than the .cw-body tan: that tone was chosen against the flat #0e0804
   screen, and the glow lifts the backdrop enough here to erode its contrast. */
.cw-menu-subtitle {
    font-size: 34px; letter-spacing: 4px; margin-top: 10px;
    color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
}

/* ---- Cast band ------------------------------------------------------------
   The four playable chickens, which are the actual product. Sprites are the
   same Stage-0 exports the character select uses, so this costs no new art. */
.cw-menu-cast {
    flex-direction: row; align-items: flex-end; justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 44px; margin-bottom: 48px;
}
.cw-menu-cast__item { align-items: center; margin-left: 26px; margin-right: 26px; }
.cw-menu-cast__art  { width: 200px; height: 200px; }
.cw-menu-cast__name {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; letter-spacing: 2px; margin-top: 10px;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center; white-space: nowrap;
    padding-left: 14px; padding-right: 14px;
}
/* The *light* class variants (--cw-class-*-light in CluckWarsTokens.uss), not the
   base tints. The base tints are tuned to sit on the flat #0e0804 screen; over the
   painted plate they land on dark green grass, where Warrior red (#C04030) and
   Assassin purple (#7B68EE) both fall below a readable ratio. Same hues, lifted. */
.cw-menu-cast__name--warrior  { color: rgb(240, 152, 136); }
.cw-menu-cast__name--speedy   { color: rgb(255, 176, 136); }
.cw-menu-cast__name--fatty    { color: rgb(255, 243, 176); }
.cw-menu-cast__name--assassin { color: rgb(196, 184, 255); }

/* ---- Actions --------------------------------------------------------------
   One primary, two secondary. Three identical pills gave the eye no entry
   point; SOLO is the instant-play path a playtester takes almost every time. */
.cw-menu-actions { align-items: center; flex-shrink: 0; }
.cw-menu-primary {
    min-width: 620px; min-height: 148px;
    font-size: 58px; letter-spacing: 4px;
}
.cw-menu-secondary-row { flex-direction: row; justify-content: center; margin-top: 20px; }
.cw-menu-secondary {
    min-width: 300px;
    font-size: 40px; letter-spacing: 2px;
    margin-left: 12px; margin-right: 12px;
}
/* PLAY AGAIN: one wood plank, label on top and the "{cls} · {perk}" sub-line under it,
   both inside the button (one touch target; the sub-line reads on wood, not on the
   backdrop). Same width as PLAY SOLO, which stays the only green CTA. Display is
   driven from C# (hidden until a valid last setup exists) - no display rule here. */
/* PLAY AGAIN sits ABOVE PLAY SOLO and, while it is shown, is the green primary (Phase 4,
   re-audit item 17): MenuUiController.RefreshPlayAgain swaps the two buttons' colour classes and
   demotes PLAY SOLO to a wood plank. */
.cw-menu-playagain { align-items: center; margin-bottom: 16px; }
.cw-menu-playagain__btn {
    min-width: 620px; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    /* The wood atom's painted plank sits inside transparent bevel/shadow margins, so the
       two lines need more inset than a one-line .cw-btn to land centred on the plank. */
    padding-top: 26px; padding-bottom: 32px;
}
.cw-menu-playagain__label {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 40px; letter-spacing: 2px; color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
    padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; -unity-text-align: middle-center;
}
.cw-menu-playagain__sub {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-ExtraBold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(254, 236, 196);
    -unity-text-outline-width: 2px; -unity-text-outline-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; -unity-text-align: middle-center;
}
/* 20:9 phones (~961 px canvas): with PLAY AGAIN shown the stack outgrew the
   height, clipping the title and pushing the solo hint off-screen. Compress
   the title and the cast band; the actions keep their full touch sizes. */
.layout--short .cw-menu-title { font-size: 104px; letter-spacing: 6px; }
.layout--short .cw-menu-subtitle { margin-top: 0; }
.layout--short .cw-menu-cast { margin-top: 14px; margin-bottom: 18px; }
.layout--short .cw-menu-cast__art { width: 150px; height: 150px; }
.layout--short .cw-menu-cast__name { margin-top: 4px; }
.layout--short .cw-menu-primary { min-height: 132px; }
.layout--short .cw-menu-secondary-row { margin-top: 14px; }
.layout--short .cw-menu-hint { margin-top: 12px; }
/* PLAY SOLO while PLAY AGAIN is the primary: a wood secondary at the HOST / JOIN size.
   Three classes so it beats .layout--short .cw-menu-primary whatever the order. */
.cw-menu .cw-menu-primary.cw-menu-primary--demoted { min-height: 116px; font-size: 44px; letter-spacing: 3px; }
.cw-menu .cw-menu-playagain__btn.cw-btn--green { min-height: 148px; }
.cw-menu .cw-menu-playagain__btn.cw-btn--green .cw-menu-playagain__label { font-size: 52px; letter-spacing: 4px; }
.cw-menu-hint {
    font-size: 32px; margin-top: 26px;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
}

/* Build stamp. Bottom-left, deliberately quiet — it exists so a tester can say
   which build a bug came from, not to be read during play. */
.cw-menu-build {
    position: absolute; left: 28px; bottom: 20px;
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 26px; letter-spacing: 1px;
    color: rgba(254, 245, 224, 0.7);
    -unity-text-outline-width: 1px; -unity-text-outline-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
}


/* ============================================================================
   PHASE 1 STRUCTURE (2026-10-06): shared page chrome + page transitions
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Every menu page is header (ribbon + HOME/BACK) / body / one green CTA.
   The root carries layout classes from MenuUiController.UpdateLayout:
     .layout--short   panel height < 1100 (16:9 at 1080, 20:9 phones: Pixel 9 canvas ~2157x961)
     .layout--narrow  aspect < 1.55 (4:3 tablets: 2048x1536 canvas ~1663x1247)
   ============================================================================ */
.cw-page-header {
    align-items: center; justify-content: center; flex-shrink: 0;
    padding-top: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; min-height: 132px;
}
.layout--short .cw-page-header { padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 2px; min-height: 120px; }
.layout--short .cw-page-header .cw-home-btn { top: 6px; }
.cw-page-footer { align-items: center; flex-shrink: 0; padding-top: 6px; padding-bottom: 18px; }
.layout--short .cw-page-footer { padding-bottom: 10px; }
.cw-page-cta { min-width: 520px; letter-spacing: 2px; }

/* Page transitions (MenuUiController.SetPage). The classes go on each page's
   TemplateContainer (.cw-pagewrap). Out: 120 ms ease-in, fade + slide away;
   in: 200 ms ease-out from the travel direction (forward = from the right).
   The --in-* classes are applied for one frame with no transition and then
   removed, so the page animates back to rest. Reduced motion skips all of it
   in C# (and .cw-reduced-motion zeroes the durations as a backstop). */
.cw-pagewrap {
    transition-property: opacity, translate;
    transition-duration: 0.2s;
    transition-timing-function: ease-out;
}
.cw-pagewrap--out { opacity: 0; transition-duration: 0.12s; transition-timing-function: ease-in; }
.cw-pagewrap--out-fwd  { translate: -72px 0; }
.cw-pagewrap--out-back { translate: 72px 0; }
.cw-pagewrap--in-fwd  { opacity: 0; translate: 110px 0; transition-duration: 0s; }
.cw-pagewrap--in-back { opacity: 0; translate: -110px 0; transition-duration: 0s; }

/* ============================================================================
   MENU JUICE  (Phase 3B; MenuJuice / MenuCountdown, timings in MenuJuicePolicy)
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Effects write inline scale / translate / opacity from C# and clear them when done,
   so the stylesheet stays the resting state. .cw-fx-live (on an element an effect
   drives) switches its transitions off so hover / selected transitions never fight
   the curve; .cw-fx-hold hides a slot's new content until the flying icon lands.
   Reduced motion: C# never starts an effect, so none of this is ever applied.
   The Fx particle classes are repeated in MatchOverlays.uss (separate sheet).
   ============================================================================ */
.cw-fx-live.cw-fx-live { transition-duration: 0s; }
.cw-fx-hold { opacity: 0; }

/* Fly-to-slot ghost: an ability icon (disc + sprite fill it) sized and moved from C#. */
.cw-fly-ghost { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 100px; height: 100px; }

/* Particles (Art/UI/Fx, white art tinted here). Anchored top-left at the burst point;
   the negative margins centre each sprite on it. */
.cw-fx-particle {
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0;
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
}
.cw-fx-sparkle {
    width: 56px; height: 56px; margin-left: -28px; margin-top: -28px;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Fx/Fx_Sparkle.png");
    -unity-background-image-tint-color: rgb(255, 214, 80);
}
.cw-fx-dust {
    width: 100px; height: 100px; margin-left: -50px; margin-top: -50px;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Fx/Fx_Dust.png");
    -unity-background-image-tint-color: rgb(255, 248, 232);
}
.cw-fx-feather-1, .cw-fx-feather-2, .cw-fx-feather-3 {
    width: 64px; height: 64px; margin-left: -32px; margin-top: -32px;
    -unity-background-image-tint-color: rgb(255, 248, 232);
}
.cw-fx-feather-1 { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Fx/Fx_Feather_1.png"); }
.cw-fx-feather-2 { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Fx/Fx_Feather_2.png"); }
.cw-fx-feather-3 { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Fx/Fx_Feather_3.png"); }

/* START MATCH 3-2-1-GO!: full-screen, never takes a tap (BACK still works while it counts). */
.cw-countdown {
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
    align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    background-color: rgba(8, 4, 2, 0.38);
}
.cw-countdown__num {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 380px; letter-spacing: 4px; color: rgb(255, 224, 120);
    -unity-text-outline-width: 14px; -unity-text-outline-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    text-shadow: 0px 14px 0px rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.9);
    -unity-text-align: middle-center; white-space: nowrap;
    padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0;
}
.cw-countdown__num--go { color: rgb(123, 227, 92); }

/* Small section heads on cream (PERK, STARTERS). */
.cw-small-head {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; letter-spacing: 2px; color: rgb(107, 74, 42);
    margin-top: 6px; margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 0; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0;
}

/* ============================================================================
   PICK YOUR BIRD  (CharacterSelectClass.uxml)
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Wide (desktop, phone): [4 portrait tiles][hero]. Narrow (4:3): tiles above
   the hero. Budget on the Pixel 9 canvas (961 tall): header 120 + footer ~142
   leaves ~699 for the body; the hero text column needs ~600 at ~800 px wide.
   ============================================================================ */
.cw-pick-body {
    flex-grow: 1; min-height: 0; flex-direction: row;
    /* padding-top keeps the selected tile's lift + glow clear of the HOME plank above it */
    padding-left: 24px; padding-right: 24px; padding-top: 30px; padding-bottom: 4px;
    width: 100%; max-width: 2240px; align-self: center;
}
.layout--narrow .cw-pick-body { flex-direction: column; }

/* Wide layouts (16:9 desktop, 20:9 phone): the four tiles are a 2x2 grid, so each tile is close to
   square and its chicken fills most of it. A single row of four made tall, narrow tiles with the
   chicken small and a dead colour field above it. Narrow (4:3) keeps one row of four. */
.cw-class-tiles { flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; align-content: stretch; flex-grow: 1; flex-basis: 0; min-width: 0; margin-right: 18px; }
.layout--narrow .cw-class-tiles { flex-wrap: nowrap; flex-grow: 0; flex-basis: auto; height: 330px; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 18px; }

/* Portrait tile: class fill (lightened tint, set in C#), ink outline, big
   chicken. Selected = gold border + CardGlowFrame + lift, never colour alone. */
.cw-class-tile {
    flex-grow: 1; flex-basis: 40%; min-width: 0;
    margin-left: 7px; margin-right: 7px; margin-top: 7px; margin-bottom: 7px;
    align-items: center; justify-content: flex-end;
    padding-top: 12px; padding-bottom: 14px; padding-left: 8px; padding-right: 8px;
    border-left-width: 5px; border-right-width: 5px; border-top-width: 5px; border-bottom-width: 5px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 24px; border-top-right-radius: 24px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 24px; border-bottom-right-radius: 24px;
    background-color: rgb(255, 248, 232);
    transition-property: scale, translate; transition-duration: 0.12s;
}
.layout--narrow .cw-class-tile { flex-basis: 0; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; }
.cw-class-tile:hover { scale: 1.02 1.02; }
/* Selected (Phase 4, re-audit items 10 + 19) = scale + gold inner border + an ink ring outside
   + a corner check badge. No translate lift: the stagger entry's inline translate ended on 0 and
   the lift then transitioned in afterwards (the "late hop"). Border WIDTH never changes, so the
   tile's content and its neighbours never shift. The check is drawn in USS (no art). */
.cw-class-tile--selected {
    scale: 1.04 1.04;
    border-left-color: rgb(245, 200, 66); border-right-color: rgb(245, 200, 66);
    border-top-color: rgb(245, 200, 66); border-bottom-color: rgb(245, 200, 66);
}
.cw-class-tile__ring {
    position: absolute; left: -11px; top: -11px; right: -11px; bottom: -11px;
    border-left-width: 6px; border-right-width: 6px; border-top-width: 6px; border-bottom-width: 6px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 30px; border-top-right-radius: 30px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 30px; border-bottom-right-radius: 30px;
    display: none;
}
.cw-class-tile__check {
    position: absolute; top: 10px; right: 10px;
    width: 60px; height: 60px;
    align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    background-color: rgb(245, 200, 66);
    border-left-width: 5px; border-right-width: 5px; border-top-width: 5px; border-bottom-width: 5px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 30px; border-top-right-radius: 30px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 30px; border-bottom-right-radius: 30px;
    display: none;
}
/* The tick: an L of two ink borders, turned 45 degrees. */
.cw-class-tile__check-mark {
    width: 16px; height: 28px; margin-top: -6px;
    rotate: 45deg;
    border-right-width: 7px; border-bottom-width: 7px;
    border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
}
.cw-class-tile--selected > .cw-class-tile__ring, .cw-class-tile--selected > .cw-class-tile__check { display: flex; }
.cw-class-tile__art { flex-grow: 1; width: 100%; min-height: 100px; -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit; }
.cw-class-tile__name {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 36px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    -unity-text-align: middle-center; white-space: nowrap; flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 6px; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0;
}
/* Ink on the lightened class fill: >= 7:1 for all four classes. */
.cw-class-tile__role {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    -unity-text-align: middle-center; white-space: nowrap; flex-shrink: 0;
    padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0;
}

/* Hero: one cream card. Stage on the left, text column on the right. */
.cw-hero {
    flex-grow: 1.5; flex-basis: 0; min-width: 0; min-height: 0;
    flex-direction: row; align-items: stretch;
    padding-top: 16px; padding-bottom: 16px; padding-left: 16px; padding-right: 22px;
}
.layout--narrow .cw-hero { flex-grow: 1; }
/* Phase 4 (re-audit item 10): stage, bale and chicken ~1.4x the Phase 1 size.
   Round-2 finding 16: a painted backdrop instead of a flat wash - the barn interior (Bg_Loadout,
   cropped to its sunlit doorway, which lands right behind the bird) multiplied by a pale class tint
   (C#), with the radial glow as a soft light on the bird; the figure is centred vertically. */
.cw-hero__stage {
    width: 460px; flex-shrink: 0; margin-right: 18px;
    align-items: center; justify-content: center; overflow: hidden;
    border-top-left-radius: 20px; border-top-right-radius: 20px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 20px; border-bottom-right-radius: 20px;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Backgrounds/Bg_Loadout.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-and-crop;
    /* class tint on the painting set in C# */
}
/* Light + bale + bird as one block, 550 tall: bale bottom at 0, the 434 px figure from 116 up. */
.cw-hero__figure { width: 460px; height: 550px; flex-shrink: 0; align-items: center; justify-content: flex-end; }
/* 4:3: the stage is ~530 tall, so the block is drawn a little smaller (from its centre). */
.layout--narrow .cw-hero__figure { scale: 0.9 0.9; }
/* Centred on the chicken's chest (~55% up the 434 px figure, whose box starts 116 px above the
   block's bottom): 116 + 0.55 * 434 - 448 / 2 = ~131. */
.cw-hero__glow { width: 448px; height: 448px; bottom: 131px; }
/* Phase 2: the hero stands on a hay bale (Frames/Pedestal_HayBale, 512x256; its top face
   spans source y 40-96, i.e. ~16-38% of the height). The chicken's feet land on that face. */
.cw-hero__platform {
    position: absolute; bottom: 0;
    width: 378px; height: 189px;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Frames/Pedestal_HayBale.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
}
/* Feet on the bale's top face: bale top = 189 * 0.73 = ~138; feet sit 5% (22 px) above the
   figure's bottom edge -> margin 116. */
.cw-hero__chicken { width: 434px; height: 434px; margin-bottom: 116px; }
/* Top-aligned (re-audit item 10): centring made the name jump whenever a class's quote / perk
   text was a line longer or shorter. */
.cw-hero__text { flex-grow: 1; flex-basis: 0; min-width: 0; justify-content: flex-start; padding-top: 8px; }
.cw-hero__name {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 60px; letter-spacing: 2px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    -unity-text-align: middle-left; white-space: nowrap;
    padding-left: 0; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; margin-bottom: 0;
}
.cw-hero__quote {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; -unity-font-style: italic; color: rgb(107, 74, 42);
    white-space: normal; padding-left: 0; margin-bottom: 6px;
}

/* Strong/weak callouts on cream: dark green / dark red, both >= 6:1 on #fff8e8.
   The +/- glyphs are separate labels so the read never depends on colour. */
.cw-role-list { width: 100%; }
.cw-role-row { flex-direction: row; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 2px; }
.cw-role-glyph {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 36px; width: 40px; flex-shrink: 0;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center; margin-right: 6px; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0;
}
.cw-role-glyph--pos, .cw-role-callout--strong { color: rgb(30, 106, 30); }
.cw-role-glyph--neg, .cw-role-callout--weak   { color: rgb(160, 40, 30); }
.cw-role-callout {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 32px; white-space: normal; flex-shrink: 1; flex-grow: 1; min-width: 0;
    padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0;
}

/* Perk badges: tap = select the perk AND show its detail (#PerkDetail).
   Selected = gold fill + thick ink border + lift. */
.cw-perk-row { flex-direction: row; align-items: stretch; flex-shrink: 0; }
.cw-perk-badge {
    flex-grow: 1; flex-basis: 0; min-width: 0; min-height: 116px;
    align-items: stretch; justify-content: flex-start;
    background-color: rgb(243, 230, 200); background-image: none;
    border-left-width: 3px; border-right-width: 3px; border-top-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-left-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.45); border-right-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.45);
    border-top-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.45); border-bottom-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.45);
    border-top-left-radius: 16px; border-top-right-radius: 16px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 16px; border-bottom-right-radius: 16px;
    padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 14px; padding-right: 14px;
    margin-left: 0; margin-right: 12px;
    transition-property: scale; transition-duration: 0.1s;
}
.cw-perk-badge:hover { scale: 1.02 1.02; }
.cw-perk-badge--selected {
    scale: 1.03 1.03;
    background-color: rgb(245, 200, 66);
    border-left-width: 5px; border-right-width: 5px; border-top-width: 5px; border-bottom-width: 5px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
}
.cw-perk-badge__name, .cw-perk-badge__line {
    flex-shrink: 0; margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;
    padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0;
    -unity-text-align: upper-left; color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
}
.cw-perk-badge__head { flex-direction: row; align-items: center; flex-shrink: 0; }
.cw-perk-badge__icon { width: 52px; height: 52px; flex-shrink: 0; margin-right: 10px; }
.cw-perk-badge__name {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 34px; letter-spacing: 1px; white-space: nowrap;
}
.cw-perk-badge__line {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; white-space: normal;
}
.cw-perk-detail {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; color: rgb(74, 48, 24); white-space: normal;
    margin-top: 8px; padding-left: 0; flex-shrink: 0;
}

/* Starters: ONE row of icon chips for the selected perk (label.starters). */
.cw-starter-row { flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; margin-top: 8px; flex-shrink: 0; }
.cw-starter-row__label { margin-right: 12px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; }
.cw-starter-chip {
    flex-direction: row; align-items: center; flex-shrink: 0;
    padding-top: 4px; padding-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 6px; padding-right: 18px;
    margin-right: 12px; margin-top: 4px; margin-bottom: 4px;
    background-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 32px; border-top-right-radius: 32px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 32px; border-bottom-right-radius: 32px;
}
.cw-starter-chip__icon { width: 56px; height: 56px; margin-right: 10px; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }
.cw-starter-chip__name {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
    padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; white-space: nowrap;
}

/* ---- Chicken figures -----------------------------------------------------
   Class figures are 1024 px renders of the real models (Phase 2,
   Art/UI/Chickens/Hero_<cls>_idle.png, made by tools/ui_capture/render_heroes.py),
   applied by adding a .cw-chicken--<class> modifier (in UXML or C#). Square,
   centred, feet ~5% above the bottom edge. */
.cw-chicken { -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit; }
.cw-chicken--warrior  { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Chickens/Hero_warrior_idle.png"); }
.cw-chicken--speedy   { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Chickens/Hero_speedy_idle.png"); }
.cw-chicken--fatty    { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Chickens/Hero_fatty_idle.png"); }
.cw-chicken--assassin { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Chickens/Hero_assassin_idle.png"); }
.cw-radial-glow {
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/RadialGlow.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    position: absolute;
}

/* ============================================================================
   ABILITY ICONS (shared by deck cards, slots, starter chips, lobby hexes)
   MenuUiController.AbilityIconView keeps ONE sprite element + ONE monogram
   label per host and swaps classes/text on refresh.
   ============================================================================ */
.cw-icon-sprite {
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
}
/* Phase 2 icons are cream silhouettes with an ink outline; on a cream card they need a
   colour behind them. The disc is the HUD's own hex (Atoms/HexGlossy) tinted with the
   ability's accent in C#, so a move looks the same in the menus and on the in-match button.
   On a lobby mini-hex the hex IS the disc, so PaintIcon(disc: false) hides it. */
.cw-icon-disc {
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/HexGlossy.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
}
.cw-icon-sprite--on-disc { left: 17%; top: 17%; right: 17%; bottom: 17%; }
/* Fallback when an ability has no authored sprite: its monogram on its accent
   disc (text colour picked against the accent in C#). Never blank. */
.cw-ability-mono {
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 22px; letter-spacing: 0;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0;
    margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;
    border-left-width: 3px; border-right-width: 3px; border-top-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 50%; border-top-right-radius: 50%;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 50%; border-bottom-right-radius: 50%;
}
.cw-ability-card__icon .cw-ability-mono { font-size: 34px; }
.cw-slot-box__icon .cw-ability-mono { font-size: 26px; }
/* On a lobby mini-hex the hex itself is the accent disc; only the text shows. */
.cw-mini-hex .cw-ability-mono {
    font-size: 22px; background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    border-left-width: 0; border-right-width: 0; border-top-width: 0; border-bottom-width: 0;
}

/* ============================================================================
   GEAR UP  (CharacterSelect.uxml)
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Slots on top, ONE deck below (two groups side by side; on 4:3 the class
   group wraps under the shared one), bottom bar = tapped move's details +
   READY. Budget, Pixel 9 canvas 961 tall: header 120 + slots ~170 + deck
   ~360 + bottom ~150 = ~800. No page scroll.
   ============================================================================ */
/* The chosen bird in the barn doorway (Phase 4 item 21, Phase 5 finding 7). It owns a layout slot:
   the doorway takes the height left between the slot row and the deck (the deck keeps its natural
   height), so the whole bird stands on the deck's top edge and no card ever covers it. The square
   render is drawn scale-to-fit, i.e. as tall as the slot and centred on the door. Too short a slot
   (4:3, where the class cards wrap to two lines) hides the bird: GearDoorway.Fits, set in C#. */
.cw-gear-doorway { flex-grow: 1; flex-shrink: 1; min-height: 0; align-items: stretch; justify-content: flex-end; }
.cw-gear-chicken {
    height: 100%; max-height: 360px;
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
}
.cw-gear-chicken--nofit { display: none; }
.cw-gear-body {
    flex-grow: 1; min-height: 0; min-width: 0;
    padding-left: 16px; padding-right: 16px; padding-bottom: 14px;
}
.layout--short .cw-gear-body { padding-bottom: 8px; }

.cw-slot-box-row { flex-direction: row; align-items: stretch; flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 30px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.cw-slot-box {
    flex-grow: 1; flex-basis: 0; min-width: 0;
    min-height: 124px;
    flex-direction: row; align-items: center; justify-content: flex-start;
    background-color: rgb(243, 230, 200); background-image: none;
    border-left-width: 4px; border-right-width: 4px; border-top-width: 4px; border-bottom-width: 4px;
    border-left-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.55); border-right-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.55);
    border-top-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.55); border-bottom-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.55);
    border-top-left-radius: 18px; border-top-right-radius: 18px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 18px; border-bottom-right-radius: 18px;
    margin-left: 8px; margin-right: 8px;
    padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 8px; padding-left: 26px; padding-right: 12px;
    transition-property: scale, translate; transition-duration: 0.12s;
}
/* Filled = Frames/Card_Cream; filled + armed = Frames/Card_CreamSelected (same geometry, gold
   glow in the margin), so arming a filled slot never shifts its contents. The art carries the
   outline: border 0 and the 4 px it took goes back into the padding. */
.cw-slot-box--filled {
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Frames/Card_Cream.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    -unity-slice-left: 40; -unity-slice-right: 40; -unity-slice-top: 40; -unity-slice-bottom: 44;
    -unity-slice-scale: 0.7px;
    border-left-width: 0; border-right-width: 0; border-top-width: 0; border-bottom-width: 0;
    padding-top: 12px; padding-bottom: 12px; padding-left: 30px; padding-right: 16px;
}
.cw-slot-box--filled.cw-slot-box--armed {
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Frames/Card_CreamSelected.png");
    border-left-width: 0; border-right-width: 0; border-top-width: 0; border-bottom-width: 0;
}
/* Armed = gold border (selection) + lift + the NEXT caret above it. */
.cw-slot-box--armed {
    scale: 1.03 1.03;
    border-left-width: 7px; border-right-width: 7px; border-top-width: 7px; border-bottom-width: 7px;
    border-left-color: rgb(245, 200, 66); border-right-color: rgb(245, 200, 66);
    border-top-color: rgb(245, 200, 66); border-bottom-color: rgb(245, 200, 66);
}
/* Slot number = the in-match button that fires it. */
.cw-slot-box__num {
    position: absolute; left: -14px; top: -14px;
    width: 46px; height: 46px;
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 28px; color: rgb(254, 245, 224); -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    background-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 23px; border-top-right-radius: 23px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 23px; border-bottom-right-radius: 23px;
    padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 2px;
}
.cw-slot-box__icon { width: 84px; height: 84px; flex-shrink: 0; margin-right: 14px; }
.cw-slot-box__texts { flex-grow: 1; flex-shrink: 1; min-width: 0; align-items: flex-start; }
.cw-slot-box__name {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 32px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12); white-space: normal;
    padding-left: 0; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; margin-left: 0; -unity-text-align: middle-left;
}
.cw-slot-box__empty-label {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(107, 74, 42);
    padding-left: 0; margin-left: 0;
}
/* NEXT caret: gold tag + pointer above the armed slot (shape + word, not colour only). */
.cw-next-caret {
    position: absolute; top: -44px; left: 50%; translate: -50% 0;
    align-items: center; display: none;
}
.cw-slot-box--caret > .cw-next-caret { display: flex; }
.cw-next-caret__label {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; letter-spacing: 2px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    background-color: rgb(245, 200, 66);
    border-left-width: 3px; border-right-width: 3px; border-top-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 12px; border-top-right-radius: 12px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 12px; border-bottom-right-radius: 12px;
    padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 2px; padding-left: 16px; padding-right: 16px;
}
.cw-next-caret__tip {
    width: 20px; height: 20px; margin-top: -12px; rotate: 45deg;
    background-color: rgb(245, 200, 66);
    border-right-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
}
/* Locked starter tag: padlock glyph + STARTER on an ink pill. */
.cw-starter-tag {
    flex-direction: row; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 4px;
    padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 2px; padding-left: 10px; padding-right: 12px;
    background-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 10px; border-top-right-radius: 10px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 10px; border-bottom-right-radius: 10px;
}
.cw-starter-tag__lock {
    width: 28px; height: 28px; margin-right: 6px; flex-shrink: 0;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Icons/Glyph_Lock.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
    -unity-background-image-tint-color: rgb(245, 200, 66);   /* cream x gold = gold on the ink pill */
}
.cw-starter-tag__text {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 28px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
    padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0;
}

/* The deck. Groups sit in one line (cards shrink a little on 16:9 rather than
   scroll). On 4:3 (.layout--narrow) the groups stay side by side and the CARDS wrap inside
   their group (four per line at 290 px): wrapping the class group under the one-card ANY BIRD
   group left a near-empty band across the middle of the page. */
.cw-deck {
    flex-grow: 0; flex-shrink: 0;
    flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: nowrap;
    justify-content: center; align-items: center; align-content: center;
}
.layout--narrow .cw-deck-cards { flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; }
.layout--narrow .cw-ability-card { width: 290px; flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 6px; margin-bottom: 6px; }
.layout--narrow #CommonRow { flex-shrink: 0; }   /* the class group absorbs the squeeze, so ANY BIRD never clips its card */
.cw-deck-group {
    flex-shrink: 1; min-width: 0;
    margin-left: 6px; margin-right: 6px; margin-top: 6px; margin-bottom: 6px;
    padding-top: 20px; padding-bottom: 20px; padding-left: 18px; padding-right: 18px;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Frames/Frame_WoodPanel.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    -unity-slice-left: 40; -unity-slice-right: 40; -unity-slice-top: 40; -unity-slice-bottom: 40;
    -unity-slice-scale: 0.75px;
}
.cw-deck-group__title {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 32px; letter-spacing: 2px; color: rgb(245, 200, 66);
    white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 6px; margin-left: 12px; padding-top: 0;
}
.cw-deck-cards { flex-direction: row; flex-shrink: 1; min-width: 0; }

/* Art-forward card: category colour as the frame + a category band on top
   (both set in C#), big icon, name. */
/* Fixed height (Phase 4, re-audit item 8): every card is the same height whether or not it carries
   a STARTER tag, so the category bands line up across both groups. Side padding keeps a long name
   off the frame; the band cancels it to stay flush. */
.cw-ability-card {
    width: 226px; flex-shrink: 1; min-width: 0; height: 290px;
    margin-left: 5px; margin-right: 5px;
    align-items: center; justify-content: flex-start;
    padding-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 10px; padding-right: 10px;
    background-color: rgb(255, 248, 232);
    border-left-width: 6px; border-right-width: 6px; border-top-width: 6px; border-bottom-width: 6px;
    border-top-left-radius: 20px; border-top-right-radius: 20px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 20px; border-bottom-right-radius: 20px;
    transition-property: scale, translate; transition-duration: 0.1s;
}
.cw-ability-card:hover { scale: 1.03 1.03; }
.cw-ability-card > .cw-glow { display: none; }
.cw-ability-card--picked > .cw-glow { display: flex; }
/* Picked = the gold glow; focused = an ink frame (colour set in C#, same width, so nothing inside
   moves). Neither scales nor lifts the card (MenuJuiceGuardTests): the old 1.03 scale + 12 px lift
   left an equipped card resting at another size and height than its row; the pop now settles at 1. */
.cw-ability-card__band {
    align-self: stretch; height: 44px; flex-shrink: 0;
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; letter-spacing: 1px; -unity-text-align: middle-left;
    padding-left: 12px; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 2px; margin-left: -10px; margin-right: -10px; margin-top: 0;
    border-top-left-radius: 13px; border-top-right-radius: 13px;
}
.cw-ability-card__icon { width: 112px; height: 112px; flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; }
.cw-ability-card__name {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; letter-spacing: -1px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12); -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    /* nowrap: a 12-letter single word (DOPPELGANGER) must never break mid-word on a
       shrunk 16:9 / 4:3 card; at -1 px tracking it fits a ~200 px card. */
    white-space: nowrap; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0;
}
/* Only a name that cannot fit the card at 30 px steps down (MenuUiController.FitCardName). */
.cw-ability-card__name--long { font-size: 26px; }
.cw-ability-card .cw-starter-tag { margin-top: 6px; }
/* Slot number on a picked card (which in-match button fires it). Fill is the
   accent, text colour picked against it in C#. */
.cw-ability-badge {
    position: absolute; top: -16px; right: -14px;
    width: 46px; height: 46px;
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 28px; color: rgb(254, 245, 224); -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 2px;
    border-left-width: 3px; border-right-width: 3px; border-top-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-left-color: rgb(26, 14, 4); border-right-color: rgb(26, 14, 4);
    border-top-color: rgb(26, 14, 4); border-bottom-color: rgb(26, 14, 4);
    border-top-left-radius: 24px; border-top-right-radius: 24px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 24px; border-bottom-right-radius: 24px;
}

/* Bottom bar: details (grows) + READY. */
.cw-gear-bottom { flex-direction: row; align-items: stretch; flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 6px; }
.cw-gear-ready { min-width: 480px; flex-shrink: 0; margin-left: 16px; letter-spacing: 3px; align-self: center; }
.cw-ability-detail {
    flex-grow: 1; flex-shrink: 1; min-width: 0; min-height: 116px;
    justify-content: center;
    padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 20px; padding-right: 20px;
    background-color: rgb(255, 248, 232);
    border-left-width: 4px; border-right-width: 4px; border-top-width: 4px; border-bottom-width: 4px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 16px; border-top-right-radius: 16px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 16px; border-bottom-right-radius: 16px;
}
.cw-ability-detail__head { flex-direction: row; align-items: center; flex-shrink: 0; }
.cw-ability-detail__name {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 34px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    white-space: nowrap; flex-shrink: 0; margin-right: 14px; padding-left: 0; margin-left: 0;
}
.cw-ability-detail__text {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 32px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    white-space: normal; flex-shrink: 1; padding-left: 0; margin-left: 0;
}
.cw-cat-tag, .cw-cd-badge {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; letter-spacing: 1px;
    padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 2px; padding-left: 12px; padding-right: 12px;
    border-top-left-radius: 8px; border-top-right-radius: 8px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 8px; border-bottom-right-radius: 8px;
    margin-right: 8px; flex-shrink: 0;
}
/* On cream: dark text on a pale wash, both >= 5:1. */
.cw-cd-badge--short { background-color: rgb(214, 240, 200); color: rgb(30, 96, 30); }
.cw-cd-badge--med   { background-color: rgb(250, 230, 160); color: rgb(110, 72, 0); }

/* ============================================================================
   THE COOP  (Lobby.uxml) — lineup on pedestals, rule chips, bottom bar
   ============================================================================ */
/* One ink plate behind the whole row (Phase 4, re-audit item 11): the backdrop's bunting used to
   poke through the gaps between the chips on the phone. */
.cw-rule-chips {
    flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; align-items: center;
    flex-shrink: 0; align-self: center; max-width: 96%; margin-bottom: 6px;
    padding-left: 16px; padding-right: 16px; padding-top: 6px; padding-bottom: 6px;
    background-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.82);
    border-top-left-radius: 40px; border-top-right-radius: 40px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 40px; border-bottom-right-radius: 40px;
}
.cw-rule-chips__head {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; letter-spacing: 2px; color: rgb(254, 245, 224); margin-right: 8px; margin-left: 10px;
    -unity-text-outline-width: 3px; -unity-text-outline-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    text-shadow: 0px 3px 0px rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.85);
}
.cw-rule-chip {
    flex-direction: row; align-items: center;
    background-color: rgb(255, 248, 232);
    border-left-width: 3px; border-right-width: 3px; border-top-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 26px; border-top-right-radius: 26px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 26px; border-bottom-right-radius: 26px;
    padding-top: 2px; padding-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 14px; padding-right: 14px;
    margin-left: 5px; margin-right: 5px; margin-top: 3px; margin-bottom: 3px;
}
.cw-rule-chip__k {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; color: rgb(107, 74, 42); margin-right: 10px; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0;
}
.cw-rule-chip__v {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-ExtraBold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12); padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0;
}

/* Lineup: four seats side by side; each = stage (chicken over a player-colour
   pedestal) + a cream nameplate. */
.cw-lineup {
    flex-grow: 1; min-height: 0; flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: center; align-items: stretch;
    padding-left: 18px; padding-right: 18px;
}
.cw-seat {
    flex-grow: 1; flex-basis: 0; min-width: 0; max-width: 500px;
    margin-left: 10px; margin-right: 10px;
    align-items: stretch; justify-content: flex-end;
}
.cw-seat__stage { flex-grow: 1; min-height: 120px; align-items: center; justify-content: flex-end; }
/* Phase 2: Frames/Pedestal_Ring (512x128, white art) tinted with the seat's player colour
   in C# (-unity-background-image-tint-color). */
.cw-seat__pedestal {
    position: absolute; bottom: 0;
    width: 84%; height: 84px;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Frames/Pedestal_Ring.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
}
/* Player plate on the pedestal's front (Phase 4, re-audit item 21): P1..P4 on the seat's player
   colour (fill + text colour set in C#), so two birds of one class are told apart at a glance. */
.cw-seat__pedestal-tag {
    position: absolute; bottom: 8px;
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 32px; letter-spacing: 1px; -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 2px; padding-left: 16px; padding-right: 16px;
    border-left-width: 4px; border-right-width: 4px; border-top-width: 4px; border-bottom-width: 4px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 14px; border-top-right-radius: 14px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 14px; border-bottom-right-radius: 14px;
}
.cw-seat--empty .cw-seat__pedestal-tag { display: none; }
.cw-seat__chicken { width: 92%; flex-grow: 1; max-height: 300px; margin-bottom: 26px; -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit; }
.cw-seat--empty .cw-seat__chicken { display: none; }
.cw-seat--empty .cw-seat__pedestal { opacity: 0.45; }
.cw-seat__plate {
    flex-shrink: 0; align-items: center;
    margin-top: 8px;
    padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 12px; padding-left: 12px; padding-right: 12px;
    background-color: rgb(255, 248, 232);
    border-left-width: 4px; border-right-width: 4px; border-top-width: 10px; border-bottom-width: 4px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    /* top border = player colour, set in C# */
    border-top-left-radius: 18px; border-top-right-radius: 18px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 18px; border-bottom-right-radius: 18px;
}
.cw-seat--empty .cw-seat__plate { background-color: rgba(243, 230, 200, 0.85); }
.cw-seat--you .cw-seat__plate > .cw-glow { display: flex; }
.cw-seat__plate > .cw-glow { display: none; }
.cw-seat__namerow { flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; justify-content: center; max-width: 100%; }
.cw-seat__name {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 38px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis;
    flex-shrink: 1; min-width: 0; margin-right: 10px; padding-left: 0; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0;
}
/* P-tag: ink pill, cream text, player-colour stripe on its left edge (C#). */
.cw-seat__pn {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 32px; color: rgb(254, 245, 224); flex-shrink: 0;
    background-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-left-width: 10px;
    padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 2px; padding-left: 8px; padding-right: 10px;
    margin-right: 8px; margin-top: 2px; margin-bottom: 2px;
    border-top-left-radius: 8px; border-top-right-radius: 8px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 8px; border-bottom-right-radius: 8px;
}
.cw-seat__tag {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 32px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12); flex-shrink: 0;
    background-color: rgb(243, 230, 200);
    border-left-width: 3px; border-right-width: 3px; border-top-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 8px; padding-right: 8px;
    border-top-left-radius: 8px; border-top-right-radius: 8px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 8px; border-bottom-right-radius: 8px;
}
.cw-seat__class {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; color: rgb(107, 74, 42); -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    white-space: normal; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; margin-top: 2px;
}
.cw-seat__waiting {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(107, 74, 42);
    -unity-text-align: middle-center; white-space: normal;
}
.cw-seat__hexes { flex-direction: row; justify-content: center; margin-top: 6px; flex-shrink: 0; }
.cw-mini-hex {
    width: 64px; height: 74px; margin-left: 2px; margin-right: 2px;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/HexGlossy.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
    align-items: center; justify-content: center;
}
.cw-mini-hex__icon { width: 46px; height: 46px; }
/* READY status: gold rosette badge with ink text — a status, not a button. */
.cw-seat__state {
    flex-direction: row; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    margin-top: 8px; flex-shrink: 0;
    padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 2px; padding-left: 18px; padding-right: 18px;
    background-color: rgb(245, 200, 66);
    border-left-width: 4px; border-right-width: 4px; border-top-width: 4px; border-bottom-width: 4px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 30px; border-top-right-radius: 30px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 30px; border-bottom-right-radius: 30px;
}
.cw-seat__state--picking { background-color: rgb(243, 230, 200); border-left-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.5); border-right-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.5); border-top-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.5); border-bottom-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.5); }
/* READY = Frames/Badge_Rosette (white art, tinted gold here) + the word; hidden while picking. */
.cw-seat__rosette {
    width: 44px; height: 44px; margin-left: -8px; margin-right: 6px; flex-shrink: 0;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Frames/Badge_Rosette.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
    -unity-background-image-tint-color: rgb(255, 214, 80);
}
.cw-seat__state--picking .cw-seat__rosette { display: none; }
.cw-seat__state-label {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12); padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0;
}

/* Bottom bar: status / invite / join on the left, READY! banner centre, START right. */
.cw-coop-bottom {
    flex-direction: row; align-items: center; flex-shrink: 0;
    padding-left: 24px; padding-right: 24px; padding-top: 10px; padding-bottom: 14px;
}
.layout--short .cw-coop-bottom { padding-top: 6px; padding-bottom: 8px; }
.cw-coop-left { flex-direction: row; align-items: center; flex-shrink: 1; min-width: 0; }
/* Stretched to the bar's height so the absolutely placed READY! status has a box to centre in. */
.cw-coop-center { flex-grow: 1; flex-basis: 0; min-width: 0; align-self: stretch; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }
.cw-coop-right { flex-shrink: 0; align-items: center; }
/* Menu Coop (round-2 finding 10): equal side columns, so READY! and the join card sit on the centre
   of the PAGE rather than in whatever gap the status pill and START leave. The in-match waiting
   room keeps the plain bar (its invite card + two buttons need the room). */
.cw-coop-bottom--centred > .cw-coop-left { flex-grow: 1; flex-basis: 0; }
.cw-coop-bottom--centred > .cw-coop-center { flex-grow: 0; flex-basis: auto; min-width: 480px; }
.cw-coop-bottom--centred > .cw-coop-right { flex-grow: 1; flex-basis: 0; align-items: flex-end; }
/* READY! is a status, not a control (Phase 4, re-audit item 11): outlined gold display type with
   no plank or ribbon behind it, so it can never read as a second button next to START MATCH. */
.cw-ready-banner {
    /* Over the centre of the bar, out of flow: showing / hiding it (or the stamp, with the join
       code card under it) never moves anything else. */
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
    padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 24px; padding-right: 24px;
    align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    transition-property: scale, opacity; transition-duration: 0.35s; transition-timing-function: ease-out-back;
}
.cw-ready-banner--hidden { scale: 0.4 0.4; opacity: 0; transition-duration: 0s; }
.cw-ready-banner__label { font-size: 76px; letter-spacing: 4px; color: rgb(255, 214, 80); }

/* START MATCH hand-off card: Styles/GetReadyCard.uss (shared with the in-match intro overlay). */

/* ============================================================================
   SETTINGS SHEET  (main menu gear -> modal; MainMenu.uxml #SettingsSheet)
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Replaced the two toggles that used to sit on the loadout screen (#OptionsRow),
   which cost the phone pick list ~230 px. Four rows, each a whole-row touch
   target (MenuUiController.BindSettingRow toggles on a tap anywhere in it):
   name + one-line description on the left, the checkbox on the right.

   The checked state is carried by the BOX FILL (cream -> gold) and the ink
   tick, not only by the glyph: the checkmark image comes from the default
   runtime theme, and if that ever fails to resolve a glyph-only design would
   render ON and OFF identically.
   ============================================================================ */
.cw-sheet-scrim {
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
    /* 0.62 let HOST / JOIN read through under the sheet (Phase 1 review): near-opaque now. */
    background-color: rgba(20, 10, 4, 0.88);
    align-items: center; justify-content: center;
}
.cw-sheet {
    width: 1180px; max-width: 94%; max-height: 96%;
    padding-top: 28px; padding-bottom: 32px; padding-left: 40px; padding-right: 40px;
    align-items: stretch;
}
.cw-sheet__head {
    flex-direction: row; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0; margin-bottom: 20px; min-height: 116px;
}
.cw-sheet__close { position: absolute; right: 0; top: 0; left: auto; min-width: 180px; }
.cw-sheet__body { padding-top: 10px; padding-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 22px; padding-right: 22px; flex-shrink: 1; }
.cw-setting-toggle-row {
    flex-direction: row; align-items: center;
    min-height: 116px;                        /* 48 dp floor - the whole row is the target */
    padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 8px;
    border-bottom-width: 2px; border-bottom-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.18);
}
.cw-setting-toggle-row--last { border-bottom-width: 0; }
.cw-setting-toggle-row__texts { flex-grow: 1; flex-shrink: 1; min-width: 0; margin-right: 24px; }
.cw-setting-toggle-row__name {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 40px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    white-space: nowrap; margin-left: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0;
}
.cw-setting-toggle-row__desc {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 32px; color: rgb(107, 74, 42);
    white-space: normal; margin-left: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0;
}

.cw-opt-toggle {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0;
}
/* Vertical centering ONLY. A Toggle is a BaseField, i.e. flex-direction: row -
   the theme pairs `flex-grow: 1` with `flex-basis: 0` on the input, so
   overriding grow to 0 collapses the input to zero width. Leave grow/basis. */
.cw-opt-toggle .unity-toggle__input { align-items: center; }
.cw-opt-toggle .unity-toggle__checkmark {
    width: 72px; height: 72px;
    margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0;
    background-color: rgb(243, 230, 200);
    border-left-width: 4px; border-right-width: 4px; border-top-width: 4px; border-bottom-width: 4px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 14px; border-top-right-radius: 14px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 14px; border-bottom-right-radius: 14px;
    -unity-background-image-tint-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
}
.cw-opt-toggle:checked .unity-toggle__checkmark {
    background-color: rgb(245, 200, 66);      /* gold = selected */
    -unity-background-image-tint-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
}

/* ---- Inset well + text input --------------------------------------------- */
.cw-well {
    background-color: rgba(10, 6, 2, 0.4);
    border-left-width: 2px; border-right-width: 2px; border-top-width: 2px; border-bottom-width: 2px;
    border-left-color: rgba(138, 106, 58, 0.4); border-right-color: rgba(138, 106, 58, 0.4);
    border-top-color: rgba(138, 106, 58, 0.4); border-bottom-color: rgba(138, 106, 58, 0.4);
    border-top-left-radius: 16px; border-top-right-radius: 16px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 16px; border-bottom-right-radius: 16px;
}
.cw-input {
    background-color: rgb(26, 14, 8);
    border-left-width: 3px; border-right-width: 3px; border-top-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-left-color: rgb(106, 74, 40); border-right-color: rgb(106, 74, 40);
    border-top-color: rgb(106, 74, 40); border-bottom-color: rgb(106, 74, 40);
    border-top-left-radius: 12px; border-top-right-radius: 12px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 12px; border-bottom-right-radius: 12px;
    min-height: 116px; font-size: 48px; color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
}
/* The runtime TextField paints its own light input box; make it a cream well with ink text. */
.cw-input .unity-text-field__input, .cw-input .unity-base-text-field__input {
    background-color: rgb(243, 230, 200); color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-ExtraBold.ttf");
    font-size: 44px; border-left-width: 0; border-right-width: 0; border-top-width: 0; border-bottom-width: 0;
    padding-left: 16px;
}

/* ---- Lobby bottom-bar cards (invite / join), code tiles, status ------------ */
.cw-lobby-card {
    padding-top: 16px; padding-bottom: 16px; padding-left: 20px; padding-right: 20px;
    margin-top: 14px;
}
.cw-lobby-cardlabel {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(107, 74, 42);
}
.cw-coop-left .cw-lobby-card { margin-top: 0; margin-left: 14px; padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 10px; }
/* Gold invite-code letter tiles */
.cw-code-tiles { flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 12px; }
.cw-code-tile {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 52px; color: rgb(26, 14, 4);
    background-color: rgb(212, 160, 32);
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/GlossOverlay.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    border-left-width: 2px; border-right-width: 2px; border-top-width: 2px; border-bottom-width: 2px;
    border-left-color: rgb(184, 138, 20); border-right-color: rgb(184, 138, 20);
    border-top-color: rgb(184, 138, 20); border-bottom-color: rgb(184, 138, 20);
    border-top-left-radius: 8px; border-top-right-radius: 8px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 8px; border-bottom-right-radius: 8px;
    /* Width + font set per tile by CodeTileFit (a long code shrinks its tiles, then wraps). */
    -unity-text-align: middle-center; flex-shrink: 0;
    padding-top: 4px; padding-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0;
    margin-right: 8px; margin-bottom: 8px;
}

.cw-lobby-btnrow { flex-direction: row; margin-top: 14px; }
.cw-mini-btn {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    flex-grow: 1; flex-basis: 0;
    min-height: 116px;
    font-size: 32px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Frames/Frame_WoodPanel.png");   /* wood: secondary action */
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    -unity-slice-left: 40; -unity-slice-right: 40; -unity-slice-top: 40; -unity-slice-bottom: 40;
    -unity-slice-scale: 0.6px;
    border-left-width: 0; border-right-width: 0; border-top-width: 0; border-bottom-width: 0;
    padding-top: 12px; padding-bottom: 16px; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0;
    margin-right: 12px;
}
.cw-lobby-btnrow { align-items: center; margin-top: 4px; }
.cw-lobby-btnrow .cw-code-tiles { margin-top: 0; margin-right: 8px; flex-wrap: nowrap; }
.cw-lobby-btnrow .cw-mini-btn { flex-grow: 0; flex-basis: auto; min-width: 140px; margin-right: 0; margin-left: 10px; }
/* Join (Phase 4, re-audit item 9): the code entry is centred in the bottom bar under the open
   gate, big and centred; JOIN MATCH stays a disabled wood plank until the code is complete. */
.cw-join-card { align-items: center; padding-top: 6px; padding-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 24px; padding-right: 24px; }
.cw-join-card .cw-lobby-cardlabel { -unity-text-align: middle-center; }
.cw-join-card .cw-input { margin-top: 6px; min-width: 560px; }
.cw-join-card .cw-input .unity-text-field__input, .cw-join-card .cw-input .unity-base-text-field__input {
    font-size: 64px; letter-spacing: 10px; -unity-text-align: middle-center; padding-left: 0;
}
/* Round-2 finding 10. 20:9 phone: a lower entry and more bar padding, so the card ends well clear of
   the screen's bottom edge (it ended 9 px from it). 4:3: a narrower entry, so the page-centred card
   stays clear of START / JOIN MATCH in the right column. */
.layout--short .cw-coop-bottom--centred { padding-bottom: 20px; }
.layout--short .cw-join-card .cw-input { min-height: 92px; }
.layout--short .cw-join-card .cw-input .unity-text-field__input, .layout--short .cw-join-card .cw-input .unity-base-text-field__input { font-size: 56px; }
.layout--narrow .cw-join-card .cw-input { min-width: 440px; }

/* Status pill */
/* Status line: cream inset, dark text (the status colour is set in C# from
   dark greens/browns that clear 4.5:1 on #f3e6c8). */
.cw-status-pill {
    flex-direction: row; align-items: center; margin-top: 16px;
    padding-top: 12px; padding-bottom: 12px; padding-left: 18px; padding-right: 18px;
    background-color: rgb(243, 230, 200);
    border-left-width: 4px; border-right-width: 4px; border-top-width: 4px; border-bottom-width: 4px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 10px; border-top-right-radius: 10px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 10px; border-bottom-right-radius: 10px;
}
.cw-status-dot {
    width: 20px; height: 20px; margin-right: 14px;
    border-top-left-radius: 10px; border-top-right-radius: 10px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 10px; border-bottom-right-radius: 10px;
    background-color: rgb(245, 200, 66);
    border-left-width: 2px; border-right-width: 2px; border-top-width: 2px; border-bottom-width: 2px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
}
.cw-status-count {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 34px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12); margin-right: 12px;
}
.cw-status-text {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 32px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12); flex-grow: 1; -unity-text-align: middle-right;
}
.cw-coop-left .cw-status-pill { margin-top: 0; }
.cw-lobby-error {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    margin-top: 10px; min-height: 38px; font-size: 32px;
    color: rgb(255, 150, 140); -unity-text-align: middle-center; white-space: normal;
    -unity-text-outline-width: 2px; -unity-text-outline-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
}

/* ---- Responsive ---------------------------------------------------------- */
.layout--portrait  .cw-mode-row { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; }
.layout--landscape .cw-mode-row { flex-direction: row; justify-content: center; }

/* ============================================================================
   ABILITY ICON SPRITES  (37 : type-name -> Icons/Abilities/Icon_<TypeName>.png)
   One rule per AbilityIconStyle.ByType entry, kept identical in CluckWarsTheme.uss
   and TouchControls.uss (AbilityIconArtTests checks every class, file and url).
   Cream silhouettes with an ink outline on transparent: the coloured hex / accent
   disc behind them supplies the colour (menu overhaul Phase 2).
   ============================================================================ */
